{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790327666,"nonce":"h/LIv3Rxj0veT80zVE1C3F/Vyyw=","title":"wasm backend refuses integer comparisons and a loop phi that passes itself along","message":"`emit_binary_op` in crates/compiler/src/wasm_backend.rs had arms for integer arithmetic and for the float comparisons only, so any function comparing integers (`Eq`, `Ne`, `Lt`, `Le`, `Gt`, `Ge`) or using the bitwise ops failed with \"wasm-jit can't lower: binary op Gt on I64\" and stayed in bytecode. Separately, the phi-cycle check in `emit_multi_block` refused a phi whose incoming on a back edge is its own result (a variable a `continue` path leaves unchanged), although copying a value onto itself cannot clobber another phi's read.\n\nFound running the block-value control-flow reproducers (crates/compiler/tests/block_value_control_flow.rs) on the wasm leg: 17 of the functions refused on comparisons, and the three `while ... continue` cases on the self-referencing phi.","files":null}]}